sti"}, {"word": "liūdėti"}, {"word": "liūdinti"}], "wikipedia": ["Rick Derksen"], "etymology_text": "From *lud-, the zero-grade of Proto-Indo-European *lewd-.\nCognate with Proto-Slavic *lȗdъ (“crazy, foolish”) < *loud-; compare Serbo-Croatian lȗd (“crazy, immature”), Russian archaic луд (lud, “stupid, crazy”). If this *lewd is the same root (to bend) as in Gothic 𐌻𐌹𐌿𐍄𐍃 (liuts, “deceitful”), Old English lūtan (“bend, stoop”), Old Norse lúta (“bow, submit”), the semantic shift may be explained as \"to bend\" > \"bring down, humble\" > \"depress\".\nThe palatalisation of the l must be due to the influence of an unattested e-grade *liaud-.", "etymology_templates": [{"name": "root", "args": {"1": "lt", "2": "ine-pro", "3": "*lewd-"}, "expansion": ""}, {"name": "der", "args": {"1": "lt", "2": "ine-pro", "3": "*lewd-"}, "expansion": "Proto-Indo-European *lewd-"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "sla-pro", "2": "*ludъ", "3": "*lȗdъ", "4": "crazy, foolish"}, "expansion": "Proto-Slavic *lȗdъ (“crazy, foolish”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "sh", "2": "lȗd", "3": "", "4": "crazy, immature"}, "expansion": "Serbo-Croatian lȗd (“crazy, immature”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "ru", "2": "-"}, "expansion": "Russian"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "got", "2": "𐌻𐌹𐌿𐍄𐍃", "3": "", "4": "deceitful"}, "expansion": "Gothic 𐌻𐌹𐌿𐍄𐍃 (liuts, “deceitful”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "ang", "2": "lūtan", "3": "", "4": "bend, stoop"}, "expansion": "Old English lūtan (“bend, stoop”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "non", "2": "lúta", "3": "", "4": "bow, submit"}, "expansion": "Old Norse lúta (“bow, submit”)"}], "word": "liūdnas", "lang": "Lithuanian", "lang_code": "lt"}